# Margince skill

Margince works from your AI tool in two ways. You can connect the tool to Margince and sign in
once, with no passport to copy or renew. Or you can give a script or your own code an agent
passport and this skill. Either way the tool works as you, and can do only what you can do.

## Connect your AI tool
{{if .MCPURL}}
This is the address an AI tool connects to:

```text
{{.MCPURL}}
```

The steps below match **Settings → AI access** in Margince. Each tool also has its own guide,
linked under its steps.

<!-- connect: claude-company -->
### Claude, through your company

Your Claude owner adds Margince once for the whole team:

1. In Claude, open the admin settings, then "Connectors".
2. Choose "Add", then "Custom", then "Web".
3. Name it Margince and paste the address above.
4. Choose "Add". Then everyone on the team connects and signs in as themselves.

Then everyone on the team:

1. In Claude, opens "Customize", then "Connectors".
2. Finds Margince and chooses "Connect".
3. Signs in to Margince and chooses "Authorize".

Claude's guide: https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11175166-get-started-with-custom-connectors-using-remote-mcp

<!-- connect: claude-own -->
### Claude, on a plan you pay for

1. In Claude, open "Customize", then "Connectors".
2. Choose "Add custom connector" and paste the address above.
3. Margince opens. Sign in and choose "Authorize".

On the Free plan, Claude allows one custom connector.

Claude's guide: https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11175166-get-started-with-custom-connectors-using-remote-mcp

<!-- connect: chatgpt-company -->
### ChatGPT, through your company

Your ChatGPT admin adds Margince once for your company:

1. In the ChatGPT admin settings, turn on "Developer mode".
2. Create an app named Margince with the address above, and choose OAuth for sign-in.
3. Publish the app so everyone in your company can turn it on.

Then everyone, in a chat, opens the + menu, turns on Margince, signs in to Margince and
chooses "Authorize".

OpenAI's guide: https://help.openai.com/en/articles/12584461-developer-mode-apps-and-full-mcp-connectors-in-chatgpt-beta

<!-- connect: chatgpt-own -->
### ChatGPT, on a plan you pay for

1. In ChatGPT, open "Settings", then "Apps & Connectors", and turn on "Developer mode".
2. Choose "Create" and paste the address above.
3. Margince opens. Sign in and choose "Authorize".

On Plus and Pro, ChatGPT can look things up in Margince but not change them.

OpenAI's guide: https://help.openai.com/en/articles/12584461-developer-mode-apps-and-full-mcp-connectors-in-chatgpt-beta

<!-- connect: copilot-company -->
### Microsoft Copilot, through your company

Someone at your company adds Margince to a Copilot agent once:

1. In Copilot Studio, open the agent, then "Tools", "Add a tool", "New tool" and
   "Model Context Protocol".
2. Name it Margince and paste the address above.
3. Under authentication choose "OAuth 2.0", then "Dynamic discovery", and choose "Create".
4. Choose "Add to agent", then publish the agent to Microsoft 365 Copilot and Teams.

Your company's data policies for connectors also apply to Margince. Then everyone opens
Copilot in Teams or Microsoft 365, chooses the agent with Margince, and signs in to Margince
when it asks.

Microsoft's guide: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/mcp-add-existing-server-to-agent

